# 2026-09-04 -- context-only refresh for the 7.2 series. No semantic change.
#
# CachyOS moved to 7.2 while linux-surface's newest tag is still arch-6.19.8-3
# (its patches/ tops out at 6.19), so this fallback hand-rebase is what builds.
# Every scheduled run from 2026-08-18 onward aborted on a single hunk:
#
#   include/linux/pci.h @509 -- adds no_shutdown:1 to struct pci_dev
#
# The field itself is unchanged upstream; only the comment on the adjacent
# context line moved:
#   -   /* BARs can't be mapped to user-space  */
#   +   /* BARs can't be mapped by CPU or peers */
# patch's fuzz cannot absorb that: fuzz trims context from the outer ends
# inward, and this is the innermost leading context line.
#
# Checked before changing it:
#   - torvalds/linux v7.2 and master still do NOT define no_shutdown, so the
#     hunk is still required. This is not upstream catching up.
#   - Full dry-run against cachyos-7.2.3-2: 92 files, 0 failures, 0 rejects,
#     0 hunks needing fuzz (50 applied at an offset, which is expected).
#   - No duplicate definitions introduced across the 46 modified files, and no
#     added enum constant collides with an existing raw value -- the two ways a
#     clean `patch` exit has silently broken this build before.
#
# RESOLVED 2026-09-10: that refresh is now build- AND boot-validated.
# cachyos-7.2.3-2 compiled clean in ~4 h on the TrueNAS builder and published
# as linux-cachyos-surface-latest 7.2.3-1, and the Surface Laptop 4 has since
# been running 7.2.3-1-cachyos-surface-latest. validated_against is therefore
# bumped from cachyos-7.1.3 to cachyos-7.2.3-2. (The 7.2.3 bump was written on
# 2026-09-04 but never committed; this is that bump, with the boot caveat it
# carried now closed.)

# 2026-09-10 -- semantic fix for cachyos-7.2.4-1: our Bluetooth quirk bit
# collided with a new upstream one. THIS IS NOT A CONTEXT-ONLY REFRESH.
#
# Every scheduled run from 2026-09-09 onward aborted on a single hunk:
#
#   drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c @67 -- adds BTUSB_LOWER_LESCAN_INTERVAL
#
# 7.2.4 added its own quirk bit in exactly the slot ours used:
#
#   #define BTUSB_BARROT			BIT(28)
#   #define BTUSB_BROKEN_EXT_SCAN		BIT(29)   <- new upstream, 7.2.4
#
# Our patch appended BTUSB_LOWER_LESCAN_INTERVAL as BIT(29). The reject is the
# safety net working as intended: had patch absorbed this with fuzz, the tree
# would have compiled with TWO different quirk macros both equal to BIT(29),
# so every 0x1286:0x204c Marvell card would also have been treated as
# BTUSB_BROKEN_EXT_SCAN and vice versa. That is precisely the "added constant
# collides with an existing raw value" failure the 2026-09-04 note lists.
#
# Fix: ours moves to BIT(30), and the hunk's context now carries upstream's
# BIT(29) line. BIT(30) and BIT(31) were both free in 7.2.4; driver_info is a
# kernel_ulong_t, so there is plenty of room left.
#
# Checked before changing it:
#   - Pristine 7.2.4 has neither the 0x1286:0x204c device entry nor any
#     le_scan_interval/le_scan_window handling, so the quirk is still required.
#     This is not upstream catching up.
#   - Full apply against a pristine cachyos-7.2.4-1 tree, with dkms-clang.patch
#     applied first exactly as prepare() does: 92 files, 0 failures, 0 rejects,
#     0 hunks needing fuzz (51 applied at an offset, which is expected). Also
#     passes with `patch -F0`, which tolerates no fuzz at all.
#   - No duplicate BTUSB_* BIT() value remains in btusb.c, and the only
#     duplicate #define names anywhere in the 92 patched files
#     (header.S, pci-me.c, pci-driver.c, pci.h) are byte-identical to pristine
#     -- pre-existing #ifdef/#else pairs upstream, not introduced here.
#
# WATCH OUT when hand-editing a hunk: keep the leading and trailing context
# BALANCED. The first attempt at this fix added upstream's BIT(29) line as a
# 4th leading context line while leaving 3 trailing, and re-numbered the
# header to @@ -67,7 +67,8 @@. That hunk is a perfectly valid unified diff --
# `git apply --check` accepts it -- but GNU patch, which is what prepare()
# actually runs, then applied it "with fuzz 1" and failed outright under -F0.
# A hunk regenerated with `diff -U3` (3 leading, 3 trailing, header
# @@ -68,6 +68,7 @@) applies with zero fuzz. Generate replacement hunks with
# diff rather than renumbering the header by hand.
#
# NOT build-validated on 7.2.4 yet: the patch set applies perfectly, but no
# 7.2.4 kernel has been compiled or booted. validated_against deliberately
# stays at cachyos-7.2.3-2 until one has; bump it then.
